{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1542877-question-about-scions-with-two-god-parents","id":1542877,"title":"Question about Scions with two God parents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-29T13:39:40-07:00","id":1542877,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Question about Scions with two God parents","content":"Born Scions are framed as chidlren of a God and a mortal. But many Gods in myth have two God parents: Ares has Zeus and Hera, Horus has Osiris and Isis, Baldr has Odin and Frigg... How does that work? Do they count as Born Scions? Do children of full divine heritage still need to start out as a mortal Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T14:23:27-07:00","id":1542879,"title":"","content":"They would start out however the story needed them to, if the game is beginning at origin level then they should begin as mortal heroes, on the other hand if it's a demigod game then congrats you're a demigod. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T15:19:04-07:00","id":1542881,"title":"","content":"Look some people clearly take after one parent more than the other. :3<br /> <br /> As far as the actual game goes, it can run a number of ways. Example an incarnation of Ares resulting from an incarnation of Zeus and Hera getting together and just part of the cycle. In which case born or incarnation are the most likely. A created could easily be something like Hephaestus making a child to fulfill Aphrodite's current need for the job and just letting her do the job of bringing it to life so she could handle any odds and ends that he didn't know about or had improperly prioritized. <br /> <br /> Other than that there's also not a hard and fast rule for the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T16:18:02-07:00","id":1542882,"title":"","content":"You can always steal from the Disney version of Hercules. Just have fate decree the child will be raised by foster parents. The kid can still be the child of two deities, maybe Hermes had a rare hetero fling with Brigid, or Columbia had a passionate experience with with a Glooskap. Either way the cross pantheon child with have to prove themselves in a different way to Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-29-2024, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T19:01:06-07:00","id":1543132,"title":"","content":"In certain cultures and traditions (but increasingly all over the place as pagans get together and compare notes), there is the concept of 'horsing' as a significant aspect of how gods and mortals interact and engage with one another. You might decide that, rather than do the incarnation stuff (or having a god become cursed as in the Hercules example), the scion has two divine parents who happened to meet, have intercourse, and produce a child during such an event. This would tie the scion to two separate gods, who were still ultimately &quot;human&quot; while things were taking place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T13:13:05-07:00","id":1543157,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd have them start out as a mortal, then go through the Hero-to-God progression; but when they attain Apotheosis, it's possible that the World may retroactively decide that they've always been that way.<br /> <br /> The reason I would do it this way is because Scion doesn't have rules for low-Legend Gods; and rather than giving a newborn Scion Legend 9 or working out rules for what a Legend 1 God would look like, I'd just keep the character at mortal pre-Visitation, Hero until Legend 5, and Demigod until Legend 9, just like everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-05-2024, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T08:55:58-07:00","id":1543583,"title":"","content":"I'd personally just have this be born a god, but without all the stuff a Legend 9 PC would be expected to possess. They're also only playable if the entire party is already Legend 9+, they just don't have the deep ties to the world that to me define Heroes and Demigods.<br /> <br /> Part of it is just me finding Born Scions by far the least interesting of the four types. But there's also no need to bother with what a newborn god is like if they're not on screen, and to my knowledge it fits the mythos better than Athena springing fully formed from Zeus's head as a mortal Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T09:06:09-07:00","id":1543584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1542877-question-about-scions-with-two-god-parents?p=1543583#post1543583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally just have this be born a god, but without all the stuff a Legend 9 PC would be expected to possess. They're also only playable if the entire party is already Legend 9+, they just don't have the deep ties to the world that to me define Heroes and Demigods.<br /> <br /> Part of it is just me finding Born Scions by far the least interesting of the four types. But there's also no need to bother with what a newborn god is like if they're not on screen, and to my knowledge it fits the mythos better than Athena springing fully formed from Zeus's head as a mortal Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically I believe Metis was a titan, but that's splitting hairs. Hephaestus however, was born a god, but was taught to be a smith by mortals, so mythologically it can happen that someone is born a god to god parents, but of a mortal tier and only be able to assume their full divinity later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T15:49:17-07:00","id":1551205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1542877-question-about-scions-with-two-god-parents?p=1543157#post1543157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd have them start out as a mortal, then go through the Hero-to-God progression; but when they attain Apotheosis, it's possible that the World may retroactively decide that they've always been that way.<br /> <br /> The reason I would do it this way is because Scion doesn't have rules for low-Legend Gods; and rather than giving a newborn Scion Legend 9 or working out rules for what a Legend 1 God would look like, I'd just keep the character at mortal pre-Visitation, Hero until Legend 5, and Demigod until Legend 9, just like everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I'd approach it. Gods take definition and legend from their deeds, and being born, fundamentally, isn't particularly mythic in itself. Building up legend and forming your Mantle is how you get written into myth. <br /> <br /> If you're the children of Gods and never achieve even Demigod-hood, there's a solid chance that you just end up forgotten in time like the millions upon millions who live and die all the time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}